WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.136
Hi, I'm Chai!

00:00:02.136 --> 00:00:03.827
Attention has a zoo of variants.

00:00:03.827 --> 00:00:07.211
Know which bill each one pays, and the zoo becomes a map.

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:14.220
Plain attention runs up two bills: an N by N score matrix,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.307
and a key-value cache that grows with context and depth.

00:00:19.942 --> 00:00:22.980
Every query scores every key, and blends the values.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.476
Every query dotted with every key.

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:27.898
Double the context, and the work quadruples.

00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:31.440
The root scale keeps softmax out of a near one-hot corner.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.995
An encoder reads every pair, in both directions.

00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:37.762
That's the full quadratic bill.

00:00:38.182 --> 00:00:41.716
A decoder masks the future: half the square, still quadratic.

00:00:42.136 --> 00:00:45.814
A sliding window reads only recent keys and caps the cache.

00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:47.486
Stacked layers compound its reach.

00:00:47.906 --> 00:00:51.541
Native sparse attention lets each query score the past cheaply, and read

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:53.056
only the blocks that matter.

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:58.791
Grouped-query attention keeps every query head, but groups them onto a

00:00:58.791 --> 00:01:00.191
few shared key-value heads.

00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:05.305
Latent attention compresses instead: keys and values become one small latent, cached,

00:01:05.305 --> 00:01:07.652
and projected back up when needed.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.911
FlashAttention keeps a tile of queries in fast on-chip memory.

00:01:13.331 --> 00:01:15.056
Key and value tiles stream past it.

00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:20.915
An online softmax tracks a running max and sum, so the answer is exact.

00:01:21.335 --> 00:01:23.928
The N by N matrix never touches slow memory.

00:01:28.017 --> 00:01:31.007
Place any new mechanism on those two axes, and you know most

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:32.751
of what it does, and gives up.

00:01:36.817 --> 00:01:41.027
So: masks cut the matrix, sharing and latents shrink the cache, and

00:01:41.027 --> 00:01:42.431
FlashAttention moves fewer bytes.

00:01:42.851 --> 00:01:44.842
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.842 --> 00:01:45.411
I'm Chai.

00:01:45.411 --> 00:01:45.696
Bye!
